# Ajuda da Rede vIRCio para InspIRCd 4.

<alias text="HELPOP" replace="HELP $2-">

<helpmsg nohelp="No help for that topic. Nao existe ajuda para este topico.">

<helptopic key="start" title="vIRCio Help" value="
Commands and modes available on the network.
Comandos e modos disponiveis na rede.

/HELP CUSER    User commands. Comandos de usuario.
/HELP COPER    Oper commands. Comandos de IRCop.
/HELP UMODES   User modes. Modos de usuario.
/HELP CHMODES  Channel modes. Modos de canal.
/HELP STATS    Server statistics. Estatisticas do servidor.
/HELP SNOMASKS Server notices. Avisos para IRCops.
/HELP EXTBANS  Extended bans. Bans estendidos.
">

<helptopic key="cuser" title="User Commands" value="
ACCEPT      ADMIN       AWAY        COMMANDS    CYCLE       HEXIP
INFO        INVITE      IRCOPS      ISON        JOIN        KICK
KNOCK       LINKS       LIST        LUSERS      MAP         MODE
MONITOR     MOTD        NAMES       NICK        NOTICE      OPER
PART        PASS        PING        PONG        PRIVMSG     QUIT
REMOVE      RMODE       SERVLIST    SETNAME     SILENCE     SQUERY
SSLINFO     STATS       TBAN        TIME        TITLE       TOPIC
UNINVITE    USER        USERHOST    VERSION     VHOST       WATCH
WHO         WHOIS       WHOWAS
">

<helptopic key="coper" title="Oper Commands" value="
ALLTIME     CBAN        CHECK       CHGHOST     CHGIDENT    CHGNAME
CLONES      CLOAK       CONNECT     DIE         DNSBL       ELINE
FILTER      GLINE       GLOADMODULE GLOBOPS     GRELOADMODULE
GUNLOADMODULE JUMPSERVER KILL       KLINE       LOADMODULE  LOCKSERV
MKPASSWD    NICKLOCK    NICKUNLOCK  OJOIN       OPERMOTD    PRETENDUSER
QLINE       RCONNECT    REHASH      RELOADMODULE RESTART    RLINE
RSQUIT      SAJOIN      SAKICK      SAMODE      SANICK      SAPART
SAQUIT      SATOPIC     SETHOST     SETIDENT    SETIDLE     SHUN
SQUIT       SWHOIS      TLINE       UNLOADMODULE UNLOCKSERV WALLOPS
XCOPY       XCOUNT      XREMOVE     XSEARCH     ZLINE
">

<helptopic key="messaging" title="Messaging Commands" value="
/PRIVMSG <target>[,<target>]+ :<message>
Sends a message to a user or channel. Envia mensagem para usuario ou canal.

/NOTICE <target>[,<target>]+ :<message>
Sends a notice to a user or channel. Envia aviso para usuario ou canal.

Rapid changes between many targets are limited to reduce spam.
Mudancas rapidas entre muitos destinos sao limitadas contra spam.
">

<helptopic key="channels" title="Channel Commands" value="
/JOIN <channel>[,<channel>]+ [<key>[,<key>]+]   Joins channels. Entra em canais.
/PART <channel>[,<channel>]+ [:<reason>]        Leaves channels. Sai de canais.
/KICK <channel> <nick> [:<reason>]              Removes a channel member.
/TOPIC <channel> [:<topic>]                     Views or sets a topic.
/NAMES [<channel>] and /LIST [<pattern>]        List channels or members.
/INVITE [<nick> <channel> [<time>]]             Invites, or lists pending invites.
/TBAN <channel> <duration> <banmask>            Sets a timed channel ban.
/REMOVE <channel> <nick> [:<reason>]            Removes a member when authorised.
/RMODE <channel> <mode> [<pattern>]             Removes matching list/prefix modes.
">

<helptopic key="who" title="/WHO <pattern> [<flags>][%<fields>[,<querytype>]]" value="
Looks up users matching a pattern. Fields request WHOX output.
Consulta usuarios por padrao. Campos solicitam resposta WHOX.

Match flags: a account, h host, i IP, m modes, n nick, r realname,
s server, u username, A away, f remote, l local, o oper, x sensitive data.

WHOX fields: a account, c common channel, d distance, f flags, h host,
i IP, l idle, n nick, o rank, r realname, s server, t query type, u username.
Sensitive data requires the appropriate oper privilege.
Dados sensiveis exigem o privilegio de IRCop adequado.
">

<helptopic key="lookup" title="User and Server Lookup" value="
/WHOIS [<servername>] <nick>[,<nick>]+  Shows user information.
/WHOWAS <nick> [<count>]                 Shows recently seen users.
/ISON <nick> [<nick>]+                   Shows online nicknames.
/USERHOST <nick> [<nick>]+               Shows nickname and host data.
/ADMIN, /INFO, /VERSION, /TIME, /MOTD    Show server information.
/LINKS, /MAP and /LUSERS                 Show network topology and counts.
">

<helptopic key="session" title="Session Commands" value="
/NICK <newnick>          Changes your nickname. Altera seu apelido.
/QUIT [:<message>]       Ends your session. Encerra sua sessao.
/AWAY [:<message>]       Sets or removes away status. Define ou remove ausencia.
/PING <cookie> [server]  Tests server response. Testa a resposta do servidor.
/PASS and /USER are sent by IRC clients during registration.
/PASS e /USER sao enviados pelo cliente durante o registro.
">

<helptopic key="privacy" title="Privacy and Notifications" value="
/ACCEPT manages the callerid list used with user mode +g.
/SILENCE manages a server-side ignore list.
/MONITOR and /WATCH monitor nickname availability.
/SSLINFO [channel|nick] shows TLS information.
/SETNAME changes your real name. /VHOST and /TITLE use configured credentials.
">

<helptopic key="ircops" title="/IRCOPS" value="
Shows online network staff ordered by administrative level, then nickname.
Mostra a equipe online por nivel administrativo e depois apelido.

Non-oper Helpers appear with level 20 when they have user mode +h, or are
@op or higher in #Help, #Ajuda, or #vIRCio. Channel halfop does not count.
Helpers nao-oper aparecem por +h de usuario ou @op/superior nesses canais.

IRCops are not listed again as Helpers. +H IRCops are hidden from normal users;
users with users/auspex can see them marked Hidden.
IRCops nao sao duplicados; users/auspex veem +H com a marca Hidden.
">

<helptopic key="helper" title="Helpers da Rede vIRCio" value="
Helpers provide user assistance and do not need to be IRCops.
Helpers atendem usuarios e nao precisam ser IRCops.

/IRCOPS recognises a non-oper Helper by +h or @op/superior in #Help, #Ajuda,
or #vIRCio. Channel +h is halfop and does not qualify.
/IRCOPS reconhece +h de usuario ou @op/superior; +h de canal e halfop.
">

<helptopic key="pretenduser" title="/PRETENDUSER <nick> :<command-line>" value="
Makes a target user execute an IRC command.
Faz o usuario alvo executar um comando IRC.

Requires PRETENDUSER command access and users/pretenduser.
Exige acesso ao comando PRETENDUSER e users/pretenduser.

You cannot target yourself, Services pseudoclients, a higher-level IRCop, or a
protected Services Root. Recursion is denied and the full payload is not logged.
Nao aceita autoalvo, pseudoclients, IRCop superior ou Root protegido.
">

<helptopic key="vircio-invisible" title="vIRCio Invisible - user mode +Q" value="
Hides a human IRCop's channel presence from viewers without users/auspex.
Oculta a presenca em canais para usuarios sem users/auspex.

JOIN/PART, NAMES, WHO and channel lines in WHOIS are hidden. Private messages
to the invisible IRCop are rejected as no such nick/channel for those viewers.
JOIN/PART, NAMES, WHO e canais no WHOIS ficam ocultos para esses usuarios.

+Q does not silence the IRCop: channel messages still work. Services and
users/auspex can see the presence. This is a user mode, not channel mode +Q.
+Q nao silencia o IRCop; Services e users/auspex continuam vendo.
">

<helptopic key="vircio-root" title="vIRCio Services Root Protection" value="
Protects human Services Roots with level 100+ and users/vircio-root.
Protege Services Roots humanos com nivel 100+ e users/vircio-root.

Protection denies KILL, KICK, REMOVE, prefix removal, SAJOIN, SAKICK, SAMODE,
SANICK, SAPART, SAQUIT and PRETENDUSER by other users.
Impede essas acoes forcadas por outros usuarios.
">

<helptopic key="vircio-zombie" title="vIRCio Zombie/Gringo - user mode +Z" value="
Places an unauthenticated user in quarantine. Coloca usuario sem conta em quarentena.

While active, the user is limited to #vIRCio and Services pseudoclients; normal
JOINs elsewhere and messages to other targets are blocked.
Enquanto ativo, limita a #vIRCio e aos Services.

Only Services can manage +Z. Account login removes it automatically.
Somente Services administra +Z; login de conta o remove.
">

<helptopic key="filter" title="/FILTER <pattern> [<action> <flags> [<duration>] :<reason>]" value="
Adds a global regex filter; with only <pattern>, removes that filter.
Adiciona filtro regex global; somente <pattern> remove o filtro.

Actions: none logs only; warn allows and notifies FILTER snomask; block denies
and notifies; silent denies without oper notice; kill disconnects; gline, zline
and shun apply the corresponding X-Line for <duration>.

Flags: p PRIVMSG, n NOTICE, P PART, q QUIT, o exclude IRCops, r exclude
registered users, c strip formatting, * all except r, - none.
">

<helptopic key="xlinetools" title="X-Line Tools" value="
/XCOUNT <criteria> counts matching X-Lines. Conta X-Lines correspondentes.
/XSEARCH <criteria> lists matching X-Lines. Lista X-Lines correspondentes.
/XREMOVE <criteria> removes matching X-Lines. Remove X-Lines correspondentes.
/XCOPY <type> <oldmask> <newmask> [options] copies an X-Line.

Criteria include -type, -mask, -reason, -source, -set, -duration, -expires,
and -config. Broad criteria can affect multiple X-Lines.
Critérios amplos podem afetar varias X-Lines.
">

<helptopic key="xlines" title="X-Lines" value="
/KLINE user@host  Local user@host ban. Ban local por usuario@host.
/GLINE user@host  Global user@host ban. Ban global por usuario@host.
/ZLINE ipmask     Global IP ban. Ban global por IP.
/QLINE nickmask   Global nickname ban. Ban global por apelido.
/ELINE user@host  Exception to matching bans. Excecao de ban.
/RLINE regex      Global regex ban. Ban global por regex.
/SHUN mask        Server-side global ignore. Ignora comandos no servidor.

One parameter removes an existing X-Line; adding one accepts an optional duration
and reason. Durations use forms such as 1d2h30m.
Um parametro remove; para adicionar use duracao e motivo quando aplicavel.
">

<helptopic key="operadmin" title="Oper Administration" value="
/CHECK target [server]      Detailed user, host, IP, or channel information.
/CLONES limit               IP/CIDR ranges with at least limit connections.
/JUMPSERVER ...             Redirects users to another server.
/LOCKSERV [:reason]         Blocks new local connections; /UNLOCKSERV reopens.
/OJOIN channel              Joins on official network business.
/REHASH [mask]              Reloads configuration on matching servers.
/LOADMODULE, /UNLOADMODULE, /RELOADMODULE manage local modules.
/GLOADMODULE, /GUNLOADMODULE, /GRELOADMODULE manage linked servers.
/CONNECT, /SQUIT, /RCONNECT and /RSQUIT manage server links.
/DIE and /RESTART control the local daemon and require elevated access.
">

<helptopic key="sa" title="SA Commands" value="
/SAJOIN [nick] channel       Forces a join. Forca entrada.
/SAPART nick channel         Forces a part. Forca saida.
/SAKICK channel nick         Forces a kick. Forca expulsao.
/SAMODE target modes         Applies a mode change. Aplica modo forcado.
/SANICK nick newnick         Changes a nick. Altera apelido.
/SAQUIT nick reason          Forces a quit. Forca desconexao.
/SATOPIC channel topic       Sets a topic. Define topic.
Protected Services Roots cannot be targets of forced administrative actions.
">

<helptopic key="stats" title="/STATS <symbol> [<servername>]" value="
Shows server statistics; access depends on configuration and oper privileges.
Mostra estatisticas; o acesso depende da configuracao e dos privilegios.

e/g/k/q/R/Z  E/G/K/Q/R/Z-Lines       s filters       C channel bans
H shuns       c links                d DNSBL         i connect classes
m commands    o oper accounts        O oper types    p listeners
u uptime      z memory               P online IRCops T bandwidth/socket
U Services    X configured unlinked servers
All /STATS use is announced to IRCops.
O uso de /STATS e anunciado aos IRCops.
">

<helptopic key="snomasks" title="Server Notice Masks" value="
Uppercase is remote and lowercase is local where both exist.
Maiuscula indica remoto e minuscula indica local.

a unspecified events  c connections  d DNSBL  f FILTER  g GLOBOPS
j channel creation    k kills        l links  n nick changes  o oper login
q quits               r rehash       v override  w gateway IP changes
t /STATS               x X-Lines     C/D/F/G/J/K/L/N/O/Q/R/V/W/X are remote equivalents.
">

<helptopic key="umodes" title="User Modes" value="
a hide idle/signon in WHOIS       c block private messages without common channel
d deaf from channel messages      g callerid accept-list protection
h available for help              i invisible in WHO
 k Services protection            o IRC operator       r registered nickname
s <mask> server notices           w WALLOPS
x cloaked hostname                z TLS-only private messages
B bot                              D private deaf       H hideoper
I hide channels in WHOIS          L disable redirect   N no channel history
O oper override                   Q vIRCio Invisible   R block unregistered PMs
S strip formatting in PMs         T block private CTCPs W WHOIS notice
Z vIRCio Zombie quarantine

Use /HELP VIRCIO-INVISIBLE and /HELP VIRCIO-ZOMBIE for +Q and +Z.
Use /HELP HELPER for user mode +h.
">

<helptopic key="chmodes" title="Channel Modes" value="
Prefixes: +v voice, +V halfvoice, +h halfop, +o op, +a admin, +q owner,
+Y official oper join.

Lists: +b ban, +e ban exception, +I invite exception, +w autoop access.
Core: +i invite-only, +k key, +l limit, +m moderated, +n no external messages,
+p private, +r Services registered, +s secret, +t topic lock.

Restrictions: +c block colour, +C block CTCP, +d delayed messages, +f flood,
+g channel filter, +j join flood, +N no nick changes, +T no NOTICE, +U opmoderated,
+B anticaps, +E repeat, +F nick flood, +M registered users speak, +R registered join,
+S strip formatting, +z TLS-only.

Other loaded modes: +A allow invite, +D delay join, +H channel history,
+J kick no rejoin, +K no KNOCK, +L redirect, +O IRCops only, +P permanent,
+Q no kicks, +u auditorium, +X exemptions, +Z long mode names.
Channel +Q is nokicks and is unrelated to user mode +Q.
">

<helptopic key="extbans" title="Extended Bans" value="
Use named extbans in +b, +e or +I; prefix ! to invert a match.
Use extbans nomeados em +b, +e ou +I; ! inverte a correspondencia.

Matching: account:, bot:, channel:, fingerprint:, gateway:, oper:, opertype:,
realmask:, realname:, server:, unauthed:.
Acting: blockcolor:, blockinvite:, mute:, noctcp:, nokick:, nonick:, nonotice:,
opmoderated:, redirect:, stripcolor:.

Example: /MODE #canal +b account:Example
The network normalises extbans to their names.
A rede normaliza extbans para seus nomes.
">

<helptopic key="misc" title="Additional Commands" value="
/ALLTIME shows network time. /CYCLE leaves and rejoins a channel.
/CLOAK generates a cloak for host or IP. /DNSBL rechecks a user.
/HEXIP converts raw and hex gateway IP forms. /MKPASSWD creates password hashes.
/NICKLOCK and /NICKUNLOCK manage forced nicknames.
/SETHOST, /SETIDENT and /SETIDLE change your own oper identity fields.
/CHGHOST, /CHGIDENT, /CHGNAME and /SWHOIS change another user when authorised.
/OPERMOTD displays the operator MOTD. /COMMANDS lists available commands.
">
